# Commercial S3.1 final prestart parity diagnosis

Date: 2026-08-29

The first dry prestart after the successful one-time database bootstrap stopped
closed for two independent parity defects. The service database role has the
intended table DML grants but no database TEMP privilege, while the original
probe attempted to create a temporary table. Separately, the root-private
allowlist still referenced the preceding test creator rather than the S3.1
synthetic reference creator.

No privilege is broadened and the mutating database bootstrap is not repeated.
Application merge `54372b6b4e02119b7a82a9bf14b417e2307fb38d`, tree
`e1662cc9e373bf85b82cd4a280da87c367f86975`, replaces the TEMP probe with a
rollback-only no-op DML probe, bounds lock/statement waits and requires the
exact synthetic creator binding.

Control permits one hash-bound allowlist repair only after validating the
existing recovery archive, stopped service, immutable historical evidence,
exact old file SHA-256 and private one-binding shape. The transform preserves
the private Telegram IDs, roles and formatting and replaces only the creator
UUID. The resulting SHA-256 is fixed in SSOT. A new read-only verifier and dry
prestart must pass before evidence finalization. No service start, restart,
enablement, provider, payment, publishing or production action is authorized.
